cycle-5 · drawer-row spec alignment with cycle-4 SCOPE_SIMPLIFICATION_HIDDEN_KEYS · GUEST × IE slice
2026-11-27

Context
-------
Cycle-4 (2026-11-27) hid three rows from the right-side control drawer
via SCOPE_SIMPLIFICATION_HIDDEN_KEYS in
src/components/nex-native/control-drawer/control-drawer-client.tsx:
  · wholesale        → /nex-native/manage/wholesale
  · nex-store        → /nex-native/store
  · buying-guides    → /nex-generated/buying-guides

The sibling spec files
tests/e2e/journey-drawer-rows-{guest,buyer,signed-in-merchant}-ie.spec.ts
still enumerated those three as drawer rows, claiming drawer coverage
for routes the drawer no longer surfaces. This was a Rule-8
false-completion risk (VERIFIED claim for a surface that doesn't exist).

Cycle-5 fix
-----------
Removed the three hidden rows from the DRAWER_ROWS_* arrays in all
three spec files, updated file-header scope notes to call out the
exclusion with a cycle-4 cross-reference, and re-ran all three slices.

